                <head>265. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The First Committee of the U.N. General Assembly discussed proposals for
                    disarmament from October 13 to December 20, 1960, under four general categories:
                    general and complete disarmament, specific disarmament proposals, prevention of
                    nuclear weapons proliferation, and suspension of nuclear testing. For the major
                    statements and texts of resolutions considered by the First Committee, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Documents on Disarmament, 1960</hi>, pages 297–372. The
                    General Assembly adopted three resolutions as recommended by the First
                    Committee, Resolutions 1576–1578. For texts, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid</hi>., pages 373–375.</p>
            </div>
